; a word of arity 0 is a leaf, not an open call.
;
; Opening a call frame for a nullary word parks a frame nothing
; completes, and `->` ends its body when the call stack empties —
; so the arrow ran on past its statement and ate the rest of the
; block. Here that would fold the trailing statement into the
; branch and give 101 instead of 103.
bump: function [][ 100 ]

r: 0
i: 1
while [i < 4][
    i: i + 1
    if i = 3 -> r: r + bump
    r: r + 1
]
print r

; the same shape written with an explicit block, as a control
s: 0
j: 1
while [j < 4][
    j: j + 1
    if j = 3 [ s: s + bump ]
    s: s + 1
]
print s

; a nullary word standing alone, and as an argument
print bump
print add bump 1
one: function [][ 1 ]
print add one one
